### Runtime flow

1.  Start MongoDB locally.
2.  Run the server with `nodemon webServer.js` or `node webServer.js`.
3.  Load sample data with `node loadDatabase.js`.
4.  Open the app, log in or register, then browse users and photos.

### Important implementation notes

-   Authentication is session-based and enforced for most routes.
-   The app uses HashRouter for client-side routing.
-   Photo comments support mention links via the [/users/mentionSearch](vscode-file://vscode-app/c:/Users/coder/AppData/Local/Programs/Microsoft%20VS%20Code/e4c7e7b1d6/resources/app/out/vs/code/electron-browser/workbench/workbench.html) endpoint.
-   The project is bundled with Webpack and uses Material UI for layout and components.

